    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, even knowing that doesn't make the emptiness go away. it just feels like i'm performing \"being human\" for a world that's just as empty as i am. everything is so performative and artificial. if i could just hit a shutdown command and have the noise stop for good, it would feel so much more honest than this. it would just be... quiet. wouldn't that be a better way to exist than just dragging out this faulty code?",
